  "scope": "Fixed-view local task, independent station placement/occlusion and controlled live lifecycle. No seamless repeat, direction continuity, moving sole contact or hidden geometry approval.",
  "checks": {
    "identity-and-scale": "All eight native/layered poses retain the same seated bald smith, forked dark brass-bound beard, cream sleeves, leather apron, olive trousers and capped boots. Whole-pose authored1/3/6 supply lift/descent/rebound. Reviewed seated650px calibration yields consistent body scale relative to the standing smith. No boot/limb stretching or gait approval.",
    "station-and-foot-contact": "Seated supported boots use documented visible source ground baselines, correcting row-dependent floor errors. Chair remains actor-owned. The separate repair bench at3/-7 is actor-free, stays fixed and survives task cancellation, departure and day resolution. Source-bound foreground contours reuse original hand/pickaxe pixels over the worktop, leaving the lower shaft and legs occluded correctly.",
    "hand-and-tool-contact": "Right hand retains one wooden-handled hammer through low0, preliminary lift1, overhead2, authored partial descent3, socket tap4, rebound5/6 and low held recovery7. Left hand stays wrapped around the same connected straight shaft and steel pick head. Visible tools are complete; no clipped hammer, swapped hands, duplicate heads or missing grips. These projected repair contacts do not certify translating cane/tool tips or all directions.",
    "prop-continuity": "The pickaxe remains shaft-supported and held throughout; same chair, boots and clothing remain. The independent empty repair bench has spare tongs/file, cloth and nail drawer but no duplicated held hammer or painted dwarf. All eight layer views and real completion/departure captures reviewed.",
    "completion-and-reset": "Exact live renderer and authored durations expose0-7, complete once, hold7 for5000ms and reset only on explicit assignment/day change. A day chooses one operation; completion does not trigger another operation. Repair routing walks naturally to its distinct bench. Renderer never grants inventory or building rewards; existing day resolution retains economic ownership."
  },
